  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An electric dipole with dipole moment <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math> is held fixed at the origin <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> in the presence of an uniform electric field of magnitude <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> If the potential is constant on a circle of radius <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> centered at the origin as shown in figure, then the correct statement(s) is/are:<br/>( <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is permittivity of free space, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>></mo><mo>></mo></math> dipole size)<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0019_2271ef8af93e.png\"/></p>"
  },
